    "lawCode": "Amd §1210, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5121\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to extending the\nauthorization of the county of Onondaga to impose an additional rate\nof sales and compensating use taxes\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nTo extend the current authorization for Onondaga County to impose an\nadditional 1% sales tax rate through November 30, 2011.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection 1. -- Authorizes Onondaga County to continue, by local law,\nthe additional 1 % Sales Tax rate through November 30,2011.\n\nSection 2. -- Provides for the distribution of funds raised by the\nadditional rate of tax among units of local government in the County.\n\nSection 3 -- Effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe Onondaga County Legislature has approved a Resolution requesting\nan extension of authorization to impose an additional 1% local Sales\nTax rate. This legislation extends such authorization for a local law\nthrough November 30, 2011.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone to New York State.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
